  "title": "Controllable Crowd Generation and Trajectory Prediction via World-Model Planning",
  "summary": "Ctrl-CWM integrates crowd generation and run-time control to simulate human behavior in real-world scenarios, while a novel cluster-based approach enables efficient dense crowd trajectory prediction. This approach addresses the limitations of existing methods by adapting the world-model principle of planning using imagined futures.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Ctrl-CWM introduces a multi-agent Controllable Crowd World Model that adapts the world-model principle to crowd simulation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The project uses a novel cluster-based approach to efficiently handle dense crowd scenarios by grouping individuals based on attributes over time.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ctrl-CWM demonstrates superior performance in crowd realism and collision avoidance compared to existing methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
